    <name>
      <text>Question 1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>An angle was measured to the nearest degree as {@ang@}\(^\circ\). Calculate:</p>
<ol style="list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0;">
  <li><p>(a) The absolute error of the stated angle.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p></li>
  <li><p>(b) The maximum possible value of the stated angle.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p></li>
  <li><p>(c) The minimum possible value of the stated angle.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p></li>
  <li><p>(d) The relative error of the stated angle.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</p></li>
  <li><p>(e) The percentage error.</p>
      <p>[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</p></li>
</ol>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The angle was measured to the nearest degree as {@ang@}\(^\circ\).</p>

<ol style="list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0;">
  <li><p>(a) <strong>Absolute error:</strong></p>
      <p>Since the angle is measured to the nearest whole degree, the absolute error is half of the smallest unit (1\(^\circ\)).</p>
      <p>\[ \text{Absolute error} = \frac{1}{2} = {@ta1@} \]</p></li>

  <li><p>(b) <strong>Maximum possible value:</strong></p>
      <p>\[ \text{Maximum value} = {@ang@} + {@ta1@} = {@ta2@} \]</p></li>

  <li><p>(c) <strong>Minimum possible value:</strong></p>
      <p>\[ \text{Minimum value} = {@ang@} - {@ta1@} = {@ta3@} \]</p></li>

  <li><p>(d) <strong>Relative error:</strong></p>
      <p>\[ \text{Relative error} = \frac{\text{absolute error}}{\text{working value}} = \frac{{@ta1@}}{{@ang@}} \approx {@ta4@} \]</p></li>

  <li><p>(e) <strong>Percentage error:</strong></p>
      <p>\[ \text{Percentage error} = \frac{\text{absolute error}}{\text{working value}} \times 100\% = {@ta4@} \times 100\% = {@ta5@}\% \]</p></li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
